{
  "name": "google-breakpad",
  "description": "Google Breakpad is a comprehensive multi-platform crash-reporting system that implements client-side minidump generation and server-side stackwalking for post-mortem analysis. It provides robust libraries for capturing process state across Linux, Windows, and macOS, utilizing platform-specific primitives such as Mach IPC, ptrace, and structured exception handling. The framework includes a sophisticated processor capable of resolving symbolic information from DWARF, STABS, and PDB formats to reconstruct human-readable backtraces from binary memory dumps.",
